course: dictionary
lesson: 9823
title: Sweeteners and food labels
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sweetener is something added to food or drink to make it taste sweet. Many sweeteners are used instead of sugar, so a drink can taste sweet with very little sugar in it.
explain: «One can of ordinary cola has about seven teaspoons of sugar; diet drinks use sweeteners with almost no sugar.» The word sweeteners tells you the diet drink tastes sweet without the sugar. Context clues like this help you understand the word.
explain: Sweetener has a second meaning: something extra offered to make a deal or idea more attractive. When someone says «as a sweetener», they are adding a small bonus to persuade you. Read the sentence around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A sweetener is something put in food or drink to make it taste sweet.
fact: «Sugar-free» drinks often contain artificial sweeteners, so check the label.
fact: Honey and syrup are natural sweeteners.
fact: «Xylitol» is a sweetener that is poisonous to dogs and cats, so keep it away from pets.
fact: As a sweetener, the word can mean a small bonus offered to make a deal more attractive.
exercise: «Diet drinks use sweeteners with almost no sugar.» What is a sweetener in this sentence? | A bag of heavy sugar | A sour sort of juice | A kind of fizzy bubble | *Something added to make a drink taste sweet
exercise: Which of these is a natural sweetener? | Salt | Vinegar | *Honey | Pepper
exercise: Dad says, «I'll cook your favourite pudding as a sweetener.» What does sweetener mean here? | A bitter herb | *A little bonus to make you agree | A dessert with lots of sugar | A type of sugar-free drink
test: Why must «chocolate, grapes and the sweetener xylitol» be kept away from a dog? | *It can poison dogs, sometimes badly enough to kill them | It makes dogs grow very big very fast | It makes dogs sleepy for a long nap | Dogs only eat them when they are hungry
test: On a «sugar-free» drink label, what might you find listed instead of sugar? | Lots of raisins | *Artificial sweeteners | Chewing gum base | Salt and vinegar
exam: Why does «sugar-free» on a drink label not mean the drink has no sweet taste? | It contains only water | *It contains sweeteners that make it taste sweet | It is always sour | It contains more sugar than cola
